    {
      "id": "r20261101-a02",
      "title": "The Secret Life of Houseplants",
      "level": "Menengah atas",
      "min": 4,
      "body": [
        "Houseplants are popular again. In big cities, many young people fill their small apartments with green plants, and plant shops are busier than ever. But why do people love plants so much?",
        "Science offers some answers. Studies show that being near plants can lower stress and blood pressure. Plants also clean the air by absorbing harmful chemicals. For people who work from home, caring for plants gives a healthy break from screens. Watering, cutting old leaves, and watching new leaves grow can be surprisingly satisfying.",
        "There is also a social side. Plant lovers trade cuttings, share advice in online groups, and even give plants as gifts. In a fast digital world, plants grow slowly, and maybe that is exactly the point: they teach us patience."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "houseplants": "tanaman hias",
        "apartments": "apartemen",
        "blood pressure": "tekanan darah",
        "absorbing": "menyerap",
        "satisfying": "memuaskan",
        "cuttings": "stek",
        "patience": "kesabaran"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
